Subject: Cantor Supervised Local Lifecycle Requirement Matrix

@ [canonical] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Supervised_Local_Lifecycle.sop
@ [slice] C:\Project\Cantor\feature_support\slices\SupervisedLocalLifecycle.sop

& [MatrixIdentity] is implementation support accounting
  + [matrix_uuid] is 3d5e6fba-c8aa-4ec5-afe0-0685cff535fc
  + [status] is complete_with_evidence

& [SLL-001] is strict artifact and state validation
  + [evidence] is strict path helpers, exact state properties, unknown-property rejection, regular-file and reparse-point rejection, and module-level validation

& [SLL-002] is hidden launch and readiness
  + [evidence] is real cantord hidden-process launch, distinct logs, state only after authenticated cantorctl status, and failed-readiness nonpublication

& [SLL-003] is atomic secret-free state
  + [evidence] is exact schema assertion, BOM-free same-directory atomic publication, and token plus auth-token-name absence scan

& [SLL-004] is complete process identity
  + [evidence] is PID plus executable plus exact start-time matching and forged-start-time health and stop rejection

& [SLL-005] is authenticated health
  + [evidence] is fresh real cantorctl status and strict machine JSON with current generation

& [SLL-006] is graceful exact stop
  + [evidence] is current-generation shutdown, confirmed exit, state removal, and listener rebinding

& [SLL-007] is safe faults
  + [evidence] is concurrent-start single-winner serialization, duplicate live refusal, stale default refusal, explicit stale replacement, forged identity rejection, failed readiness cleanup, and state preservation

& [SLL-008] is production-binary lifecycle
  + [evidence] is production_binaries_have_pid_safe_supervised_operator_lifecycle

& [SLL-009] is authority non-expansion
  + [evidence] is no tool-surface change, no model call, no automatic restart, no force kill, no semantic operation, and no tracked secret
